WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.004 --> 00:00:24.871
"Wow, this store is Ally thought as she entered Everything Mart and grabbed a shopping basket.

2
00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:28.112
"It looks like they really do sell everything here!"

3
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.241
Ally headed first for the hardware department.

4
00:00:33.261 --> 00:00:41.543
"Hmm I see hammers, nails, plywood, and paint, but no fuel cells or spaceship parts.

5
00:00:41.963 --> 00:00:43.523
I guess I'd better ask for some help."

6
00:00:44.224 --> 00:00:46.244
Ally spotted a teenager stocking the shelves.

7
00:00:46.264 --> 00:00:50.585
"Excuse me," she said.

8
00:00:50.605 --> 00:00:53.766
"Can you please tell me where I can find beta-booster coils?"

9
00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:57.047
"Huh?" The boy scratched his chin.

10
00:00:57.067 --> 00:01:00.648
"I never heard of those, but I just started working here.

11
00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.261
Let me check the inventory."

12
00:01:02.821 --> 00:01:04.983
He pulled out a handheld device and did a quick search.

13
00:01:05.003 --> 00:01:06.404
"Found it!"

14
00:01:06.744 --> 00:01:07.324
he exclaimed.

15
00:01:07.344 --> 00:01:09.346
"You're in the wrong department.

16
00:01:09.786 --> 00:01:11.247
Beta boosters are in aisle 34."

17
00:01:11.327 --> 00:01:15.490
"Phew!" Ally thought in relief.

18
00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.172
"I was worried they might not have what I need."

19
00:01:18.932 --> 00:01:20.393
She thanked the worker and headed over.

20
00:01:21.894 --> 00:01:26.217
In aisle 34 Ally was thrilled to see that the shelves were stocked with all kinds of space

21
00:01:26.297 --> 00:01:29.900
items like lasers, comm devices, and even spacesuits and helmets.

22
00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:32.821
"This is more like it!"

23
00:01:33.201 --> 00:01:33.621
she said.

24
00:01:34.842 --> 00:01:37.543
Ally walked up and down the aisle, searching for the things she needed.

25
00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:40.125
"Where are they?"

26
00:01:40.465 --> 00:01:40.985
she murmured.

27
00:01:41.626 --> 00:01:46.648
Just as disappointment began to creep in, she spotted a crowded bottom shelf marked "Clearance Items."

28
00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:54.993
a strange way to store parts," she thought, rummaging through the stuff on the shelf.

29
00:01:55.013 --> 00:01:58.094
"But humans certainly do have a lot of strange habits."

30
00:01:59.095 --> 00:02:01.096
Ally carefully began pulling things off the shelf.

31
00:02:01.504 --> 00:02:04.346
They were mostly broken comm devices and a few banged-up helmets.

32
00:02:06.008 --> 00:02:09.170
But then she spotted a gleaming silver canister marked "Fuel."

33
00:02:14.394 --> 00:02:17.156
she cried as she placed the fuel cell into her shopping basket.

34
00:02:17.176 --> 00:02:23.240
"Finally!" Ally kept looking through the items on the shelf, but she didn't see anything else that she

35
00:02:23.301 --> 00:02:27.584
needed. "At least I've got some fuel," she thought.

36
00:02:27.992 --> 00:02:32.173
"When I'm back in the pod, I'll check with Alpha, but this fuel cell could probably get us

37
00:02:32.233 --> 00:02:32.893
halfway home."

38
00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:37.955
Ally was about to go to the checkout line when she spotted something familiar on a nearby shelf.

39
00:02:38.715 --> 00:02:40.736
It was a small replica of her escape pod.

40
00:02:41.496 --> 00:02:43.256
Amazed, Ally pulled it off the shelf.

41
00:02:43.276 --> 00:02:45.677
"How could this be?"

42
00:02:48.998 --> 00:02:51.419
She blinked when she finally realized what she was holding.

43
00:02:52.819 --> 00:02:53.459
She groaned.

44
00:02:54.319 --> 00:02:56.240
"It's just a toy!"

45
00:02:58.312 --> 00:03:01.434
She yanked the fuel cell out of the shopping basket and looked at it more closely.

46
00:03:02.054 --> 00:03:03.055
"And so is this!

47
00:03:03.555 --> 00:03:04.856
These are all toys!"

48
00:03:05.436 --> 00:03:06.436
Her shoulders slumped.

49
00:03:06.457 --> 00:03:09.318
"I thought they had everything here!"

50
00:03:09.338 --> 00:03:11.799
A store manager walked by.

51
00:03:11.819 --> 00:03:17.422
"Is there something I can help you with, miss?"

52
00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:18.163
he asked.

53
00:03:18.183 --> 00:03:19.704
"Yes, please!"

54
00:03:20.084 --> 00:03:20.544
Ally said.

55
00:03:20.564 --> 00:03:23.986
"I'm looking for beta-booster coils and fuel cells.

56
00:03:24.466 --> 00:03:27.468
A clerk told me they'd be in aisle 34, but they're not here."

57
00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:32.910
"I apologize for the inconvenience," the manager said.

58
00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:37.632
"We just hired some new staff, and they're still learning about the store."

59
00:03:38.412 --> 00:03:39.773
He lowered his voice and chuckled.

60
00:03:39.793 --> 00:03:46.035
"Everyone knows that beta boosters are in the health food section!"

61
00:03:47.736 --> 00:03:48.396
Ally frowned.

62
00:03:48.416 --> 00:03:51.677
"Hmm. That doesn't sound quite right.

63
00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:54.258
Beta-booster coils aren't a healthy food.

64
00:03:54.479 --> 00:03:56.199
They're parts for a spaceship engine."

65
00:03:56.219 --> 00:03:59.881
"Oh." The manager gave her an odd look.

66
00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:06.605
"Then I have another suggestion—try the Sandville UFO Museum gift shop."

67
00:04:06.625 --> 00:04:10.126
"Argh!" Ally thought in frustration.

68
00:04:10.587 --> 00:04:12.268
"I'm just going in circles!"

69
00:04:13.028 --> 00:04:14.269
She glanced up at a clock.

70
00:04:14.289 --> 00:04:17.550
"And now I've run out of time."

71
00:04:18.131 --> 00:04:20.292
She had to get to the diner to start training Barry.

72
00:04:25.004 --> 00:04:28.745
Barry followed Ally around for the first part of her shift as she waited on customers.

73
00:04:29.345 --> 00:04:32.246
After a couple of hours, she handed him his own apron and pad.

74
00:04:32.266 --> 00:04:36.887
"I think you're ready to serve customers on your own now," she said.

75
00:04:36.907 --> 00:04:39.068
"Why don't you take table five's order?"

76
00:04:39.088 --> 00:04:46.090
"Okay!" While Barry took care of the customers, Ally waited for Ray to finish cooking some Beta Burganas

77
00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:47.030
for one of her tables.

78
00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:51.051
"How did Flo do this morning?"

79
00:04:51.371 --> 00:04:51.831
she asked.

80
00:04:51.851 --> 00:04:54.132
"Fine." Ray sighed.

81
00:04:54.748 --> 00:04:56.769
"The customers really like her."

82
00:04:56.789 --> 00:04:58.730
"That's wonderful!"

83
00:04:59.051 --> 00:04:59.531
Ally said.

84
00:04:59.551 --> 00:05:00.411
"Isn't it?"

85
00:05:00.431 --> 00:05:03.133
"Yeah, it is."

86
00:05:03.993 --> 00:05:06.455
Ray smiled as he put down the burgers for Ally's table.

87
00:05:06.835 --> 00:05:08.556
But Ally sensed that something was wrong.

88
00:05:09.336 --> 00:05:13.479
So far she'd resisted trying to read Ray's thoughts, but now she couldn't stop herself.

89
00:05:14.039 --> 00:05:17.241
And she quickly read something sad—Ray was feeling lonely.

90
00:05:17.261 --> 00:05:21.343
"The poor guy," Ally thought.

91
00:05:21.363 --> 00:05:23.104
"Work isn't everything."

92
00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.902
She served the burgers to her customers, still thinking about Ray.

93
00:05:28.302 --> 00:05:31.704
She had to come up with some ways to help him, like a true Astralian.

94
00:05:31.724 --> 00:05:36.808
"By the time I leave," Ally vowed, "he's going to be happier!"
